WEBVTT

00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:17,620
How long do I wait to recheck after my pet scan and what scan do I request?

00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:22,740
I doubt my insurance company will pay for it on a pet scan, especially since they probably

00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:29,220
only did this one because it was six months I check up after my double mastectomy and I

00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:32,380
did quite conventional treatment for the afternoons.

00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:41,010
My oncologist still has not called about my results.

00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:52,480
No, well if pet scans didn't have any ill effects, no radiation, no markers, no glucose

00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:59,320
use, etc, it would be a wonderful world and if they were free, we could just do it every

00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:06,400
week and we could see the progress objectively, our treatment for the close.

00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:12,440
However, we don't live in a perfect world and none of those things are true.

00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:17,240
So how long are you going to wait to do that on a pet scan?

00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:24,080
Well, that is dependent upon a couple of things, whether the oncologist would do it, whether

00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:29,760
your insurance would pay for it, even if you were a wealthy woman, you could, I'd say I

00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:34,760
was going to pay for it on a clock of myself, the oncologist might be stubborn and not even

00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:36,080
ordered for you.

00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:44,320
So then you have to deal with the ill effects is the pros of going by progress, more important

00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:52,760
than the ill's of radiating my body and causing damage to my body, remember, a pet scan is

00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:56,800
prevalent, I don't remember, getting like 50 chest checks, right?

00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:03,800
So you can't just pull pull that and say that that isn't, I'll be fine, if you get

00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:10,120
enough pet scans and CT scans and MRIs, you could have ill effects and that can be cancer

00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,880
causing in itself.

00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:19,240
So you've got to weigh all these things out, what's important for you to know, are there other

00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:25,760
objective tests that you can do that can give you enough data for you to be confident that

00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:30,640
you're moving in the right direction, I don't know, everybody has to make that decision

00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:36,600
for themselves, I for one don't want to get any CTs or anything.

